# Hard deploy gate

Before every push that touches `src/`, run `npx tsc -b` and `npm run lint`.
Run `npx vitest run` on every changed test file and on consumer tests that
mention any removed or renamed symbol, UI string, export, component, label,
or test ID. Search the repository with `zm-index search` or `rg` to find them.

For every deletion, rename, or API swap, search `src/` for the removed name,
label, and test ID. Update or remove stale tests asserting the old UI/API
(including layout, parent-section, and i18n tests) and old imports. Also run
`npx vitest run src/features/<area>/` for the affected feature area.

If any unit test fails locally or in CI, fix every reported failure before
pushing again, even if it seems unrelated. Any red test blocks Pages deploy.
Commit subjects must name the parent issue (`#N: ...`); CI fixes caused by
that change are follow-up commits under the same issue, not new issues.

After each push, provide the Actions run URL. Inspect its result and fix
failures from the log until the deployment build is green. Do not call the
work done or validated while its deployment is red or still running.
